    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\ngiven the text:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"aaa\"bbb\"ccc\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhen the cursor is on the middle `b`, i want to use `di\"` to delete the three `b` characters\r\nmini.ai delete three `c` characters instead\r\n\r\ni know that mini.ai groups the first and second quotation marks as one pair, and the third and fourth quotation marks as another pair\r\n\r\nbut i prefer the original, slightly dumber behavior, as it's more intuitive\r\n\r\nit is also more user-friendly for cases like `case \"$(printf \"%s\" \"$arg\")\" in...`\n\nusers can still delete the three `c` characters via next/last prefix",
